  "body": "We had a process attempt to shut down the same room using two, separate calls to the Admin API:\r\n\r\n* `DELETE /_synapse/admin/v1/rooms/{roomId}`\r\n* `POST /_synapse/admin/v1/{roomId}/delete`\r\n\r\nBoth of these method handlers eventually call [RoomShutdownHandler.shutdown_room](https://github.com/matrix-org/synapse/blob/0288e6033b08149867e742283bb0139f10b66b01/synapse/handlers/room.py#L1241), and there doesn't look to be any code that deduplicates requests anywhere.\r\n\r\nThis lead to a state where two long-running shutdown processes for the same room occurred and choked the main processes' CPU, resulting in the need to restart the main process to recover its performance.",
